# [DD-13b.W23.2] `indent_under_m.rxtin` — an indented line under an `m`
# case line, mid-block. `m` declares `children: none` (rxt_schema.def).
#
# [FINDING, w23_impl.md §3.2 vs the delivered W23.1 code] The note's
# fixture table says this class is schema-constraint; leg A's OWN
# `rxt_source.c:1169` files EVERY "indented line continues nothing" S1
# failure under RXTD_STRUCTURE regardless of WHY there was nowhere to
# attach (no parent open at all, or a parent whose `children` column is
# NONE) — MEASURED against the delivered binary. Legs B and C match leg A
# (the schema table is leg A's, §2.25.5), so all three legs refuse here,
# class structure-attachment, NAMING THE PARENT. This is S-R1's own
# detector (S239): flipping `m`'s `children` column makes leg A ACCEPT
# while legs B and C still REFUSE, so only the three-leg DIFFERENTIAL sees
# the row move, never a single leg read alone.
pattern a+
m "aaa" 0 3
  n "b"
